<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    HSK patch: gate VFE Insectoids 2 raids on the vanilla Insect
    faction by replacing the raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve so they
    don't appear in early-game / low-wealth / tribal scenarios.

    Why?
    Same problem as the Junker pirates: Megascarabs (combatPower ~30)
    are cheap enough that the storyteller can pack a few into a
    200-400 point early raid budget against a tribal start. Result:
    day-4 Norbal colony gets swarmed by hive insects.

    Note: previous attempt used <minTotalPoints> on each
    pawnGroupMaker. That field doesn't exist on PawnGroupMaker —
    RimWorld silently ignored it (XML errors in log) and the patch
    was a no-op. The correct mechanism is raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve
    on the FactionDef itself: when commonality reaches 0, the
    storyteller can't pick the faction for a raid.

    VFE I2's InsectFactionPatch.xml replaces the vanilla Insect curve
    with a soft-gate curve (300, 0) → (700, 1). That only down-weights
    — there's no hard eligibility floor, so a single Megascarab can
    still sneak into a 200-400 point early raid budget (the curve
    crossing 0 between 300 and 700 still allows non-zero commonality
    at 400+).

    Replacement curve gates at 800:
        (0, 0)        — no raids at any low budget
        (799, 0)      — still 0 right up to the threshold
        (800, 0.001)  — barely above 0 at the threshold (sharp step)
        (1400, 1.8)   — VFE's normal mid-game weight
        (2800, 2.2)   — VFE's normal late-game weight
        (4000, 2.6)   — VFE's normal end-game weight

    Infestation events are unaffected — bugs still spawn from hives in
    your colony as normal, that's a separate IncidentDef.

    LOAD ORDER NOTE: this file is named Z_HSK_* on purpose. Patches in
    the same mod's Patches/ folder run in alphabetical order. VFE I2's
    own InsectFactionPatch.xml replaces this curve too, so our patch
    must run AFTER it (Z > I) to win.
-->
<Patch>

    <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
        <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="Insect"]/raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve</xpath>
        <value>
            <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
                <points>
                    <li>(0, 0)</li>
                    <li>(799, 0)</li>
                    <li>(800, 0.001)</li>
                    <li>(1400, 1.8)</li>
                    <li>(2800, 2.2)</li>
                    <li>(4000, 2.6)</li>
                </points>
            </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
        </value>
    </Operation>

</Patch>
